# Website static (deployed via gh-pages)
# Anchored with a leading slash: these patterns describe the built dump that
# lands in the repo ROOT. Unanchored, git matches them at any depth, so they
# also swallowed the real sources under apps/website/ — index.html,
# public/manifest.json and public/og-image.* could not be committed, and the
# live site served 404s for the ones index.html references. The lone
# !/apps/queen-web/index.html below was a symptom of the same thing.
/.nojekyll
/404.html
/index.html
/docs.html
/quantum-runtime.html
/assets/
/icons/
/img/
/favicon.ico
/manifest.json
/og-image.svg
/robots.txt
/sitemap.xml
/sw.js
/vite.svg

