# Report files (auto-generated docs)
*.md
!CLAUDE.md
!.github/
!docs/**
# Queen Trinity Orchestrator Law: every container MUST carry SOUL.md at
# its root. The *.md rule above made that impossible to honour -- only
# templates/SOUL.md was re-included, so a container's own soul could never
# be committed without -f.
!**/SOUL.md
# Skills are source, not generated reports. The existing ones under
# .claude/skills/ are tracked only because they predate the *.md rule above --
# every skill written since has been silently unstageable without -f.
!.claude/skills/**
# The vendored skill corpus is a PUBLISHED artifact, exactly like
# public/t27/files: the site fetches these bodies at runtime and the manifest
# pins each one by SHA-256. The *.md rule above swallowed all 26 of them on the
# first commit, so the catalog shipped naming files that were not in the tree --
# the build passed locally, where they exist on disk, and the contract caught it
# only in CI.
!apps/website/public/skills/files/**

# Docker files in root (use deploy/ subdirectory instead)
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, because that is what the line above always
# meant. Unanchored, `Dockerfile*` matches at any depth and so it also ignored
# deploy/ — the very directory this comment tells you to use. The existing
# deploy/Dockerfile* are tracked only because they predate the rule; every one
# added since was silently untracked.
#
# deploy/Dockerfile.node is the case that surfaced it: the workflow referenced
# it, `git log` showed it in no commit, and it looked deleted. It was never
# committable.
/Dockerfile*
*.toml

# Templates (tracked for agent orchestration)
!templates/SOUL.md
fly.toml

