# Anchored 2026-09-20, same defect as website/ below. Unanchored, `extensions/`
# matched deploy/trinity-nexus/extensions at depth 3 and silently swallowed both
# browser manifests and all six icons when that tree was moved there -- the 53
# already-tracked files kept working, so nothing looked wrong, and Extension
# Release built zips with no manifest.json in them for months.
/extensions/
homebrew-tap/
install.sh
k8s/
libs/
mcp/
metrics/
models/
packages/
runtime/
translator-app/
tree-sitter-vibee/
# Anchored for the same reason: it matched deploy/trinity-nexus, where 2988
# files are tracked. No top-level trinity-nexus/ exists, so the rule was
# protecting nothing and hiding real source.
/trinity-nexus/
# website/ removed 2026-08-10: it matched apps/website at any depth and silently
# excluded every NEW file in the site source, while already-tracked files kept working.
# Build output is handled by apps/website/.gitignore (node_modules, dist).

